{'symbol': 'HON', 'date': '2020-07-24 12:30:00', 'title': 'Honeywell CEO Says Aero Business May Not Get Back To 2019 Levels Until At Least 2022', 'text': "HONEYWELL INTERNATIONAL INC SAYS COMMERCIAL AEROSPACE DECLINES WERE PARTIALLY OFFSET BY CONTINUED DEMAND FOR U.S. GOVERNMENT PROGRAMS, INCLUDING THE F-35, F-15 - CONF. CALL.HONEYWELL SAYS EXPECTS FIXED COSTS TO BE PRESSURED IN Q3 AS THE PERMANENT REDUCTIONS BEGIN TO REPLACE THE BENEFITS OF THE MORE TEMPORARY ACTIONS.HONEYWELL CFO SAYS EXPECTS 2020 CAPEX OF $900 MILLION.HONEYWELL SAYS OPEN TO DEPLOYING CAPITAL TO SHARE REPURCHASES AND M&A INVESTMENTS IN H2 IF ATTRACTIVE OPPORTUNITIES BECOME AVAILABLE.HONEYWELL CFO SAYS EXPECTS GLOBAL FLIGHT HOURS TO REMAIN SIGNIFICANTLY BELOW 2019 LEVELS.HONEYWELL SAYS COMMERCIAL ORIGINAL EQUIPMENT BUSINESS WILL CONTINUE TO BE IMPACTED BY LOWER AIR TRANSPORT OEM BUILD RATES AND LOWER BUSINESS JET DEMAND.HONEYWELL SAYS WHILE THERE ARE SIGNS OF STABILIZATION IN THE MACRO ECONOMY, KEY END MARKETS REMAIN CHALLENGED AND ECONOMIC CONDITIONS FLUID.HONEYWELL EXPECTS BETWEEN $125 MILLION AND $175 MILLION OF ADDITIONAL REPOSITIONING CHARGES IN THE THIRD QUARTER TO FUND COST PROGRAMS.HONEYWELL SAYS CO REMAINS CAUTIOUS HEADING INTO H2 AS THERE ARE STILL MANY UNKNOWNS.HONEYWELL CEO SAYS EXPECTS BUSINESS AVIATION AFTERMARKET TO BE SLIGHTLY BETTER THAN IT WAS IN Q2.HONEYWELL CFO SAYS AIRLINES BEHAVIORS Haven't NECESSARILY SOLIDIFIED YET.HONEYWELL CEO SAYS Q3 IS NOT GOING TO BE DRAMATICALLY BETTER AND EXPECTS MODEST IMPROVEMENT."}
{'symbol': 'HON', 'date': '2020-07-24 09:30:00', 'title': 'Honeywell Reports Quarterly EPS Of $1.53', 'text': 'HONEYWELL REPORTS EPS OF $1.53, ADJUSTED EPS OF $1.26; DELIVERS $1.5 BILLION OF OPERATING CASH FLOW.HONEYWELL - DELIVERED $500 MILLION OF COST SAVINGS IN QUARTER.HONEYWELL - Q2 SIGNIFICANTLY IMPACTED BY COVID-19 PANDEMIC AND OIL PRICE VOLATILITY.HONEYWELL - EXPECTS ONGOING TOP-LINE CHALLENGES DUE TO CURRENT MARKET CONDITIONS, PARTICULARLY IN AEROSPACE AND OIL AND GAS SECTORS.HONEYWELL - DEVELOPED SECOND PHASE OF COST ACTIONS COMBINED WITH PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED PLAN, WILL GENERATE $1.4 BILLION TO $1.6 BILLION OF COST SAVINGS IN 2020.HONEYWELL - QTRLY SALES $7,477 MILLION VERSUS $9,243 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.HONEYWELL - QTRLY AEROSPACE SEGMENT SALES $2,543 MILLION VERSUS $3,508 MILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.HONEYWELL - QTRLY SEGMENT MARGIN 18.5% VERSUS. 21.3% REPORTED LAST YEAR.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.21, REVENUE VIEW $7.29 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.HONEYWELL - SALES FOR SECOND QUARTER WERE DOWN 19% ON A REPORTED BASIS AND DOWN 18% ON AN ORGANIC BASIS.HONEYWELL - Q2 AEROSPACE SALES DOWN DUE TO LOWER COMMERCIAL AFTERMARKET DEMAND, REDUCED VOLUMES IN COMMERCIAL ORIGINAL EQUIPMENT & 737 MAX IMPACT.'}
{'symbol': 'IEX', 'date': '2020-07-24 19:30:00', 'title': 'Idex Reports Second Quarter Results', 'text': 'IDEX REPORTS SECOND QUARTER RESULTS.Q2 SALES $561.2 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $527.9 MILLION.Q2 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.10 EXCLUDING ITEMS.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.93.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.00 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY ORDERS OF $521.9 MILLION WERE DOWN 17 PERCENT COMPARED WITH PRIOR YEAR PERIOD.GLOBAL HEALTH PANDEMIC CONTINUED TO IMPACT COMMERCIAL PERFORMANCE.RECENT ACQUISITIONS NEGATIVELY IMPACTED ADJUSTED GROSS MARGIN AND ADJUSTED OPERATING MARGIN IN QUARTER.ENDED QUARTER WITH CASH OF $746 MILLION & NEARLY $800 MILLION AVAILABLE UNDER REVOLVING CREDIT FACILITY.UNABLE TO PROVIDE DETAILED FINANCIAL GUIDANCE NOW.EXPECT Q3 ORGANIC SALES TO BE DOWN APPROXIMATELY 12 TO 17 PERCENT VERSUS PRIOR YEAR.EXPECTS MONTHS AHEAD WILL REMAIN CHALLENGING.HAS IMPLEMENTED CERTAIN COST REDUCTION ACTIONS, INCLUDING EMPLOYEE REDUCTIONS.HAS MAINTAINED TIGHT COST CONTROL ENVIRONMENT.'}
{'symbol': 'INTC', 'date': '2020-07-24 18:30:00', 'title': 'Intel Reports Q2 GAAP EPS Of $1.19', 'text': 'SECOND-QUARTER REVENUE OF $19.7 BILLION WAS UP 20 PERCENT YEAR-OVER-YEAR.SECOND-QUARTER GAAP EARNINGS-PER-SHARE (EPS) WAS $1.19.ACCELERATING 10NM PRODUCT TRANSITION; 7NM PRODUCT TRANSITION DELAYED VERSUS PRIOR EXPECTATIONS.QTRLY NON-GAAP EPS OF $1.23.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.11, REVENUE VIEW $18.55 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.EXPECTING FULL-YEAR REVENUE OF $75 BILLION; GAAP EPS OF $4.53 AND NON-GAAP EPS OF $4.85.QTRLY DCG REVENUE $7.1 BILLION, UP 43%.QTRLY RESULTS WERE DRIVEN BY STRONG SALES OF CLOUD, NOTEBOOK, MEMORY AND 5G PRODUCTS.QTRLY CCG REVENUE $9.5 BILLION, UP 7%.SEES Q3 GAAP REVENUE ABOUT $18.2 BILLION.QTRLY PC-CENTRIC BUSINESS WAS UP ON NOTEBOOK STRENGTH DRIVEN BY CONTINUED WORK- AND LEARN AT HOME DYNAMICS OF COVID-19.SEES Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE APPROXIMATELY $1.02.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.14, REVENUE VIEW $17.90 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FULL-YEAR CAPITAL SPENDING ABOUT $15 BILLION.WORK, LEARN AT HOME DYNAMICS OF COVID-19 CONTRIBUTED TO A VOLUME DECLINE IN DESKTOP FORM FACTORS AS DEMAND SHIFTED TO NOTEBOOKS IN Q2.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $4.81, REVENUE VIEW $73.86 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES Q3 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE APPROXIMATELY $1.10.IN H2 2021, EXPECTS TO DELIVER  NEW LINE OF CLIENT CPU’S WHICH WILL INCLUDE ITS FIRST 10NM-BASED DESKTOP CPU, NEW 10NM-BASED SERVER CPU.7NM-BASED CPU PRODUCT TIMING IS SHIFTING APPROXIMATELY SIX MONTHS RELATIVE TO PRIOR EXPECTATIONS.'}
